INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal='Locate single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each region×product_line monthly volume as a multiple of its own 24-month mean, report the top-3 combos with their multiples, months, and return rates, and judge whether each is real demand or channel stuffing. Output a Markdown report saved to disk with source annotations, a data table, and a conclusion.'):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute monthly volume anomaly ratios: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) group compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_volume / 24-month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/volume_anomaly_ratios.csv) → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomaly combos & fetch return rates: From the saved ratio CSV, find the top-3 (region × product_line × month) combinations with the highest volume-to-mean ratio. For each, also extract the corresponding return_rate from the original CSV. Save a small summary CSV (top3_anomalies.csv) → code_agent
4. Assess demand vs channel-stuffing: For each of the top-3 combos, compute supporting metrics from the CSV: (a) return rate in the anomaly month vs the 24-month average return rate for that combo, (b) whether the following month's volume drops sharply (reversal), (c) the ratio magnitude. Save a metrics CSV (stuffing_indicators.csv) → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded table: Write a complete Markdown report to disk (e.g. offline_data/volume_anomaly_report.md). Requirements: H1 title, at least one data table (top-3 combos with ratio, month, return rate), every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）', and a concluding paragraph judging whether each anomaly is real demand or channel stuffing. All data from local CSV only. → code_agent
